nodecode-mind-kit is a rewrite of ousiaresearch's ousiaresearch/biomimetic-brain:

  https://github.com/ousiaresearch/biomimetic-brain
  commit efbf72d0afc4dff0ab212542eed584114f88d70d
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Ousia Research (LICENSE)

brain/ is that repository's brain/ folder, unchanged: its 37 *.example.json
files, one block per subsystem plus the aggregate example. It is data:
(mind-kit:seed) copies it into the agent directory, and nothing in it is
compiled.

cell.lisp is the rewrite of scripts/generate-brain-state.py and
scripts/decision-gate.py in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract:
the same 25 subsystems with the same status rules (a file that is gone reads
missing, never stale), the same health summary and critical flags, and the
gate's 26 rules in the order docs/DECISION_GATE.md prints them, with the
same reason codes, the same exit codes (0 PROCEED, 2 CAUTION, 1 VETO), the
same quiet-hours logic (the entrainment window, else 23:00-05:30, with the
real clock as ground truth and SCN trusted only when it is fresh and does not
drift), the same confidence adjustment, and the same labelled defaults. The
two scripts are replaced by two tools, a /mind command and the manual topic,
and the fold writes brain-state.json the way the original did.

What is left out, and why: the shell and Python maintenance passes
(brain-snapshot.sh, brain-maintenance.sh, consolidate-mind.py) and their
consistency check ran on a schedule and read the harness's own cron database,
which a cell does not own; here whatever writes the subsystem files is the
agent's business, and the cell keeps the part that reads them. Also left out:
the Python test scripts, replaced by this folder's own offline test slice;
the SETUP-GUIDE, VALIDATION and NOTES prose and docs/, which the manual topic
condenses; and the repository root's SHA256SUMS and docs/, which the fold does not read.
